{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact card history head 88ca47d36aba6ac7f076fa594bdfa7094914a31d on builder/card-histories-20261104, tree 17b307e0, for request 1c7dddfb under promise bc908c9f and review request 725346a8. This approval covers the 15 paths at this head. It claims no deployment, no Goose recovery scene and no live-host result.\n\nScope. Main c44e311c is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. The head adds two commits, and the commit-message check passes for both. Source commit ee9781b3 has tree 030639b6, the gate tree. Only the note and the two manifests change after it.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- The bridge change is small and exact. A request keeps its entry after the timeout only when the caller passes `onLate`, and only `view_act` passes one. The caller still rejects once at `TOOL_WAIT_MS`. A matching late reply removes the entry and calls `onLate` once. It never resolves or rejects the expired waiter, and it never repeats the call. Teardown clears retained entries without rejecting them again and without calling `onLate`.\n- In `main.ts`, the callback checks `alive` and the requesting view, so a closed card or a different view ignores it. The `finally` block restores the cue when the late reply arrives during the uncertain-outcome reread. **Read the card again** calls `view_read` only. No timeout, RPC method, protocol revision or admission rule changes.\n- The builder's note 08e12073 limits the claim to the signed `view_act` path, and the code agrees. A `view_read` timeout throws a plain error, and `showError` already sets `readAgain` for it, so that path keeps its existing read-only button. The held reply in the archived Goose record was a `view_read`. This head therefore adds nothing to that record and claims no Goose recovery.\n- `card-history-ledger.ts` has no imports. `card-histories.ts` imports only the ledger. The fixture drives the real `AppBridge`, `viewTools` and `ViewSessions` and compares each snapshot with the ledger after every command. I loaded the generator: 99 distinct histories, 1,268 commands, 7 to 20 each. In 45 of them, a timeout comes before the release, so they exercise the late path.\n- Each of the three controls changes one source line, and each names its witness. The unchanged-source witness fails by assertion on c44e311c (1 test, 1 failure). The record keeps the inconclusive first control and both compiler-placement failures.\n- Card workflow run 41832859529 succeeds at ee9781b3 on push, with no failed step. Its steps include the check that rebuilds `generated.ts` and refuses any diff. The four rendered histories assert the counts the note states: one `view_act` call and one read-token signature after late recovery, a second signature only on the explicit retry, none on the missing view, and no cue after teardown. Card paths change only at ee9781b3, so that run covers this head under the precedent for note-only follow-ups.\n\nThe gate passed. gate.exit reads exit 0. All five stages pass: kernel, node, counting, plain and native. The counts match the note: 135 node, 56 counting, 3,911 plain with one skip, 1,078 native with two skips. before.json and after.json record head ee9781b3, tree 030639b6, a clean status and lockfile 5a717d43. receipt.json shows exit 0, unchanged source and no owned process left after 1,623.1 seconds.\n\nEvidence. The two manifests list 23 public files. All match their sizes and digests and are read-only, both SHA256SUMS files match, and the note names both manifests. The scan finds no credential. All 39 selected gate originals match. The gate's private inventory lists 2,276 files, all match, and no unlisted file exists. The ten focused private units match their inventories, with no unlisted file, and every file has mode 0400.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The retained original stays inside the bridge's existing 32-request bound, and recovery reuses `view_read`, so no new path reaches the service.\n\nSecurity: no finding. A late reply can trigger only a read-only reread. It cannot settle a waiter, repeat a signed act or revive a closed card.\n\nSimplification: no required change. One note: a retained entry whose reply never arrives holds one of the 32 slots until teardown. After 32 lost acts on one card, the card refuses new requests. The note states the shared bound, and the card is already unusable by then, so I ask for nothing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0ef0a7d2e20acf11c2ae217335cad43a084b07cd","binding":"assigned","head":"88ca47d36aba6ac7f076fa594bdfa7094914a31d","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:67d291d72d4343f774c8df650c6153ffe4324aec\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:efee8ba644308815caed75aa90b0559399670de8\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:08e120739ddb712ae9dfb959dae2af63f46cbf25\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bc908c9fe4594068de462f7d395981fcc6296d6f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:08e120739ddb712ae9dfb959dae2af63f46cbf25","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}